    dtps: "1. Risk of treatment failure — AOM in children <5 years may involve beta-lactamase producing organisms; if no response in 48-72 hours, must escalate to amoxicillin-clavulanate. 2. Inadequate analgesia — paracetamol alone may be insufficient; ibuprofen should be added as needed. 3. Parent education needed on antibiotic adherence and danger signs.",
