    dtps: "1. Chronic infection with risk of complications — CSOM can lead to intracranial abscess, meningitis, or facial nerve palsy if untreated. 2. Conductive hearing loss affecting quality of life — patient is a teacher and relies on hearing for communication. 3. Risk of cholesteatoma development if disease progresses to atticoantral type. 4. Previous self-medication with topical ciprofloxacin without proper aural toilet — may have contributed to treatment failure.",
