    demographics: "Joseph Kamau, 52-year-old male, 88 kg, Accountant from Thika",
    chiefComplaint: "Severe frontal headache, fever, and swelling above the left eye for 5 days",
    hpi: "Joseph Kamau, a 52-year-old accountant from Thika, presents with a 5-day history of severe left frontal headache, high-grade fever (39.8°C at home), and progressive swelling and redness above the left eye. Symptoms began as a 'bad cold' 2 weeks ago which partially improved, then dramatically worsened 5 days ago. Reports thick, green nasal discharge from the left nostril. Reduced visual acuity in the left eye (blurry vision). No diplopia. No vomiting. Has a history of poorly controlled Type 2 Diabetes and has been non-compliant with metformin for the past month.",
